// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'name'. Valid alternatives: ['path']
//
// `name:` on a DuckDB specification. DuckDB is the smallest grammar in the corpus -- two
// keywords, DuckDB and path -- and duckDBDatasourceSpecification admits exactly one element,
// which is optional, so `specification: DuckDB { }` parses and `specification: DuckDB { name:
// 'mydb'; }` does not.
//
// An embedded file-backed database is the case where a rewrite is most tempted to be
// generous: `name`, `database`, `databaseName` and `path` all mean the same thing to a DuckDB
// user, and three of the four are real field names in neighbouring grammars in this same
// section (MemSql has `databaseName`, Athena has `database`, Aurora has `name`). legend-engine
// accepts exactly one of them here, and the one-element alternative list says which.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::DuckDBName
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: DuckDB;
  specification: DuckDB
  {
    name: 'mydb';
  };
  auth: Test;
}
